You are performing an authorized application security assessment of a web application backend that I own and am fully permitted to test.

I will provide the backend source code as a ZIP archive.

Your task is to perform a thorough secure code review of the entire backend and identify realistic security vulnerabilities, insecure design patterns, exposed secrets, authorization flaws, unsafe data flows, and weaknesses that could impact the confidentiality, integrity, or availability of the application.

The source archive was obtained through an externally reachable behavior in my own application during authorized testing. Because of this, also investigate what code paths, configuration, deployment behavior, file-serving logic, debug functionality, backup handling, archive exposure, path traversal, static-file configuration, or other issue could have allowed backend source files to become externally accessible.

